Hey - Sunday roundup time. Quick hits on new coffee and the Tahoe snow
picture.

New coffee spots

* Estorya Coffee - Union City - grand opening was yesterday (Oct 17),
hosted by the Union City Chamber of Commerce. A brand-new East Bay stop.
31866 Alvarado Blvd, Union City, CA 94587
https://www.eventbrite.com/e/union-city-chamber-grand-opening-estorya-coffee-tickets-2002644492587

* Cere Tea (Berkeley) - just soft-opened at 2106 Shattuck Ave in the
former Happy Lemon space. Ceremonial-grade matcha, hojicha, blended ube
drinks, plus coffee. 55 Coffee Co. is also running a pop-up inside The
Saap Avenue (4395 Piedmont Ave, Oakland).
https://briefly.co/anchor/East_Bay_food/story/itani-takes-the-helm-at-delage-berkeley-gets-another-matcha-option-and-a-coffee-pop-up-lands-on-piedmont

* Rize Up - SoMa, San Francisco - the bakery just opened its first cafe
inside its production facility. Ube sourdough, coffee, and matcha.
https://www.theinfatuation.com/san-francisco/guides/new-san-francisco-restaurant-openings

Tahoe snow

Verdict: wait - early season, none of your three Epic resorts are open and
there is no meaningful snow in the 7-day forecast. Heavenly and Northstar
project a Fri, Nov 20 opening; Kirkwood projects Fri, Dec 4. The season
outlook is encouraging: Powder Bound 2026-27 calls for 98-115% of average
snowfall with a Feb-Mar peak.
https://www.onthesnow.com/california/heavenly-mountain-resort/skireport

All four new spots are already added to your Drink Tracker's Want to Try
list. Happy exploring!

- Biggie
